      "domain": "cdc.gov",
      "rank": 1
    },
    {
      "title": "CDC Recommends Flu Vaccination Every Year for Everyone 6 Months and Older",
      "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/flu/vaccines/index.htm",
      "snippet": "CDC recommends that people 65 years and older receive a flu vaccine each season, ideally in September or October, though vaccination can still be beneficial later in the season. The page explains that adults 65+ should generally receive one of the preferred higher-dose or adjuvanted flu vaccines for better protection.",
      "domain": "cdc.gov",
      "rank": 2
    },
    {
      "title": "Flu & People 65 Years and Older: What You Should Know",
      "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/flu/highrisk/65over.htm#vaccine",
      "snippet": "CDC says older adults are more likely to develop serious flu complications such as pneumonia, hospitalization, and death. For the 2024\u20132025 flu season, the agency lists Fluzone High-Dose, Flublok, and Fluad as preferred options for adults 65 years and older if available.",
      "domain": "cdc.gov",
      "rank": 3
    },
    {
      "title": "2024-2025 Influenza Vaccination Recommendations for Adults 65 Years and Older",
      "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/flu/professionals/acip/",
      "snippet": "CDC\u2019s ACIP guidance states that adults 65 years and older should receive any age-appropriate influenza vaccine, but preferential use of higher-dose or adjuvanted vaccines is recommended when available. The recommendation applies to the 2024\u20132025 flu season and is designed to improve immune response in older adults.",
      "domain": "cdc.gov",
      "rank": 4
    },
    {
      "title": "Who Needs a Flu Shot This Season?",
      "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/flu/prevent/vaccinations.htm",
      "snippet": "CDC says yearly flu vaccination is the best way to reduce the risk of flu illness and severe outcomes, especially for adults 65 years and older. The page notes that flu vaccines are updated annually and that vaccination can begin as soon as the vaccine is available, usually in late summer and fall.",
      "domain": "cdc.gov",
      "rank": 5
    }
  ],
  "query": "current CDC flu vaccine guidance adults 65 years and older 2024 2025 site:cdc.gov",
  "count": 5
}

