      "snippet": "The coefficient of variation (CV) is calculated as standard deviation divided by the mean, usually expressed as a percentage by multiplying by 100. For example, a dataset with mean 50 and standard deviation 5 has a CV of 10%. Investors and analysts use CV to compare relative volatility across assets with different scales.",
