      "snippet": "WHO\u2019s 2024 guidance says adults aged 65 years and older should receive an age-appropriate seasonal influenza vaccine every year, ideally before local flu circulation begins. The organization notes that high-dose or adjuvanted influenza vaccines may offer improved protection in older adults, who are at higher risk of severe disease and hospitalization.",
      "domain": "who.int",
