      "snippet": "Older adults account for the majority of influenza-related hospitalizations and deaths in the United States, with risk rising sharply after age 65. Experts quoted in the article note that flu vaccines are updated annually to match circulating strains, and that high-dose formulations have been studied in people 65 and older.",
