      "title": "Influenza vaccine recommendations for adults 65+ by WHO and national programs",
      "url": "https://www.immunize.org/ask-experts/topic/influenza/older-adults/",
      "snippet": "Immunize.org summarizes current recommendations that adults 65 years and older receive an influenza vaccine every year, with preference for enhanced formulations when available. The page cites studies showing high-dose quadrivalent influenza vaccine can produce stronger antibody responses than standard-dose vaccine in older adults.",
